{"id": "EUVD-2026-99021", "enisaUuid": "2ced6cca-c1a0-3935-8856-0783bd52fa35", "description": "Vifm 0.8.1-beta through 0.14.4 reuses a pre-existing IPC FIFO in the shared temporary directory without checking ownership, allowing local users to execute commands as another user. Attackers can pre-create a world-writable vifm-ipc-vifm FIFO and write IPC packets with -c and ! shell commands that execute with the victim's privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-17T00:38:50", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/SkX7Pmiofg", "https://github.com/vifm/vifm/blob/v0.14.4/src/ipc.c#L394-L443", "https://github.com/vifm/vifm/blob/v0.14.4/src/ipc.c#L866-L874", "https://github.com/vifm/vifm/releases/tag/v0.14.4", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vifm-0.8.1-beta-through-0.14.4-unverified-ipc-fifo-ownership-allows-cross-user-command-execution"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110237", "GHSA-vf53-5m97-qg59"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a7e1866-4c2d-3b78-9d75-0197c6bcf7bd", "product": {"name": "vifm", "vendor": {"name": "vifm"}}, "product_version": "0.8.1-beta \u22640.14.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "55bb0daa-33f8-35e4-95ed-f34c5c35b24f", "vendor": {"name": "vifm"}}], "isExploited": false}